  <static seed="158" source="Contrib/Valdosta/APEX_Calculus/2.5/APEX_2.5_13.pg">
    <statement><p>Compute the derivative of the given function.</p>
<p><me>f(x) = -8 \sec(10 x)</me></p>
<p><m>f'(x) =</m><fillin characters="25" name="AnSwEr0001"/>.</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-80\sec\mathopen{}\left(10x\right)\tan\mathopen{}\left(10x\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><alert> Solution:</alert> 



Use the Chain Rule with inside function <m>u = 10 x</m>
and outside function <m>y = -8\sec u</m>.



<me>\begin{array}{rcl}
    f'(x) \amp =\amp  \displaystyle\frac{dy}{du} \cdot \frac{du}{dx}\\
    \amp \amp \\
    \amp =\amp  (-8\sec u \tan u)(10) \\
    \amp =\amp  -80 \sec(10 x)\tan(10 x)
  \end{array}</me>


</solution>
